# Vercel deploy scope: Vite + React frontend only.
#
# This repo also contains a Python project (root pyproject.toml, requirements*.txt,
# api/*.py FastAPI app, hundreds of *.py modules). Vercel's auto-detector treats
# any of those as a signal to build a FastAPI serverless function alongside the
# Vite frontend, which fails because there is no FastAPI entrypoint at the
# conventional paths (api/main.py, api/index.py, etc.).
#
# Strategy: deny-by-default, then re-include only the Vite app inputs.

# Ignore everything by default
*

# Re-include only files needed to build and serve the Vite app
!index.html
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!vite.config.js
!vercel.json
!.gitignore
!src
!src/**
!public
!public/**

# Defensive explicit exclusions of Python signals, even though `*` already
# covers them. These are listed so the intent is unambiguous and so that any
# future re-include rule cannot accidentally pull them back in.
pyproject.toml
poetry.lock
requirements.txt
requirements-*.txt
setup.py
setup.cfg
Pipfile
Pipfile.lock
api/
**/*.py
